    "tmcname": "part03-Part03_15.PrintInRange",
    "title": "Print in range",
    "prompt": {
      "points": 1,
      "paragraphs": [
        "Create the method `public static void printNumbersInRange(ArrayList numbers, int lowerLimit, int upperLimit)` in the exercise template. The method prints the numbers in the given list whose values are in the range [lowerLimit, upperLimit]. A few examples of using the method are supplied below."
      ],
      "codeSnippet": "ArrayList<Integer> numbers = new ArrayList<>();\nnumbers.add(3);\nnumbers.add(2);\nnumbers.add(6);\nnumbers.add(-1);\nnumbers.add(5);\nnumbers.add(1);\n\nSystem.out.println(\"The numbers in the range [0, 5]\");\nprintNumbersInRange(numbers, 0, 5);\n\nSystem.out.println(\"The numbers in the range [3, 10]\");\nprintNumbersInRange(numbers, 3, 10);",
      "sampleOutputs": [
        {
          "caption": "Sample output",
          "lines": [
            "The numbers in the range [0, 5]",
            "3",
            "2",
            "5",
            "1",
            "The numbers in the range [3, 10]",
            "3",
            "6",
            "5"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
